From b734e51bf19c8c5297eaafd0510e40f60e00342c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:12:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(import): read named tool coordinate systems from a
 vendor STEP

A vendor tool STEP package can carry the ISO/TS 13399 3D-model
coordinate systems (PCS, MCS, CIP, CSIF, CSW / CSWx / CSWx_y), names
confirmed from the public ISO/TS 13399-303, -401 and -405 preview pages.
geometry::import::step_csys::read_tool_csys returns every named
AXIS2_PLACEMENT_3D as plain data (origin in mm by the file's length
unit, unit z and x), classified by those names. A file without them
gives a named fall-back reason; a degenerate, non-finite or ambiguous
placement is refused by name, never a panic.

Reader only: placing a body by these frames waits for #368's tool-body
model. Pinned by the tool_csys suite and three hand-written fixtures.

Refs #370

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
